% A Belgian HR software company sends employee data to service providers
% outside the European Economic Area. Under Chapter V of the GDPR a transfer
% rests on an adequacy decision for the destination (Article 45), on
% appropriate safeguards such as standard contractual clauses (Article 46),
% or, for an occasional transfer, on a derogation such as explicit consent
% (Article 49(1)(a)). The company also assesses the impact of every transfer
% that relies on the clauses, and never sends a special category of data.
% The transfers to Japan, Switzerland, a certified US provider and, by
% explicit consent, a one-off relocation in Brazil are allowed. The US
% analytics transfer carries health data and is prohibited, the Indian
% helpdesk transfer awaits its assessment, and the bulk archive in Brazil
% has no legal basis.
% Shows alternatives of a legal basis grouped by indentation, exceptions as
% "it is not the case that", and names written as definite phrases.
% The adequacy decisions are facts of this scenario, not a register of the
% decisions in force.
% Source https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2016/679/oj (Articles 9 and 44-49)

the templates are:
    *a decision* is an adequacy decision for *a country*,
    *a decision* covers only certified recipients,
    *a recipient* is certified under *a decision*,
    *a recipient* is established in *a country*,
    the company plans *a transfer* of *a data category* to *a recipient*,
    *a data category* is a special category of data,
    *a transfer* relies on standard contractual clauses,
    the transfer impact of *a transfer* is assessed,
    *a transfer* is occasional,
    the employees gave explicit consent to *a transfer*,
    *a transfer* rests on an adequacy decision,
    *a transfer* rests on appropriate safeguards,
    *a transfer* rests on a derogation,
    *a transfer* is prohibited,
    *a transfer* is allowed,
    *a transfer* awaits a transfer impact assessment,
    *a transfer* has no legal basis.

the knowledge base gdpr chapter v includes:

% Article 45: an adequacy decision for the recipient's country. A decision
% that covers only certified recipients needs the recipient's certification.
a transfer rests on an adequacy decision
    if the company plans the transfer of a category to a recipient
    and the recipient is established in a country
    and a decision is an adequacy decision for the country
    and it is not the case that
        the decision covers only certified recipients.

a transfer rests on an adequacy decision
    if the company plans the transfer of a category to a recipient
    and the recipient is established in a country
    and a decision is an adequacy decision for the country
    and the decision covers only certified recipients
    and the recipient is certified under the decision.

% Article 46, with the company's transfer impact assessment.
a transfer rests on appropriate safeguards
    if the transfer relies on standard contractual clauses
    and the transfer impact of the transfer is assessed.

% Article 49(1)(a): explicit consent to an occasional transfer.
a transfer rests on a derogation
    if the transfer is occasional
    and the employees gave explicit consent to the transfer.

% The company never transfers a special category of data (Article 9).
a transfer is prohibited
    if the company plans the transfer of a category to a recipient
    and the category is a special category of data.

a transfer is allowed
    if the transfer rests on an adequacy decision
        or the transfer rests on appropriate safeguards
        or the transfer rests on a derogation
    and it is not the case that
        the transfer is prohibited.

a transfer awaits a transfer impact assessment
    if the transfer relies on standard contractual clauses
    and it is not the case that
        the transfer impact of the transfer is assessed.

a transfer has no legal basis
    if the company plans the transfer of a category to a recipient
    and it is not the case that
        the transfer rests on an adequacy decision
    and it is not the case that
        the transfer relies on standard contractual clauses
    and it is not the case that
        the transfer rests on a derogation.

scenario planned transfers is:
    the Japan decision is an adequacy decision for Japan.
    the Swiss decision is an adequacy decision for Switzerland.
    the Data Privacy Framework is an adequacy decision for the United States.
    the Data Privacy Framework covers only certified recipients.
    the payroll provider is established in Japan.
    the pension fund is established in Switzerland.
    the support desk is established in the United States.
    the support desk is certified under the Data Privacy Framework.
    the analytics vendor is established in the United States.
    the Indian helpdesk is established in India.
    the relocation agent is established in Brazil.
    the archive host is established in Brazil.
    health data is a special category of data.
    the company plans the payroll transfer of salary data to the payroll provider.
    the company plans the pension transfer of salary data to the pension fund.
    the company plans the support transfer of contact data to the support desk.
    the company plans the analytics transfer of health data to the analytics vendor.
    the analytics transfer relies on standard contractual clauses.
    the transfer impact of the analytics transfer is assessed.
    the company plans the helpdesk transfer of contact data to the Indian helpdesk.
    the helpdesk transfer relies on standard contractual clauses.
    the company plans the relocation transfer of contact data to the relocation agent.
    the relocation transfer is occasional.
    the employees gave explicit consent to the relocation transfer.
    the company plans the archive transfer of contact data to the archive host.
    allowed expects answers ["the payroll transfer is allowed", "the pension transfer is allowed",
        "the support transfer is allowed", "the relocation transfer is allowed"].
    prohibited expects answers ["the analytics transfer is prohibited"].
    pending expects answers ["the helpdesk transfer awaits a transfer impact assessment"].
    unfounded expects answers ["the archive transfer has no legal basis"].

query allowed is:
    which transfer is allowed.

query prohibited is:
    which transfer is prohibited.

query pending is:
    which transfer awaits a transfer impact assessment.

query unfounded is:
    which transfer has no legal basis.
